        "id": 1115498
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-17T22:38:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah okay, that makes sense. Adding it as the default case and having a VTS test to make certain NONE isn\u0027t returned is probably best in the interest of reducing unintentional implementation bugs. Thanks for pointing that out!\n\nA component could support multiple curves, but I don\u0027t think that\u0027s a usecase we want to handle. Ideally everyone would support curve 25519, and hopefully we can deprecate P256 in the future entirely whenever SEs universally offer 25519 support. \n\nIn practice, anything that offered 25519 support would probably be able to trivially offer P256 support.",
      "parentUuid": "2d61724c_86effac5",
